<%# locals: (report:) %>
<%# Legend doubling as the summary: one badge per status with its count over required cells. %>
<% gap_count = report.gaps.size %>
<div class="mb-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-5 gap-y-2 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-sm shadow-sm" id="compliance_summary">
  <div class="mr-2">
    <span class="text-gray-500"><%= pluralize(report.rows.size, "person", plural: "people") %> × <%= pluralize(report.columns.size, "type") %></span>
    <span class="ml-2 font-semibold <%= gap_count.zero? ? "text-green-700" : "text-red-700" %>" data-gap-count="<%= gap_count %>">
      <%= gap_count.zero? ? "No gaps" : pluralize(gap_count, "gap") %>
    </span>
  </div>
  <dl class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-4 gap-y-2">
    <% Compliance::SEVERITY.each do |status| %>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5" data-summary-status="<%= status %>">
        <dt><%= compliance_badge(status) %></dt>
        <dd class="font-semibold tabular-nums text-gray-900"><%= report.summary.fetch(status, 0) %></dd>
      </div>
    <% end %>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5">
      <dt><%= compliance_badge(ComplianceHelper::NOT_REQUIRED) %></dt>
      <dd class="text-gray-500">Not required for that role</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
  <p class="w-full text-xs text-gray-500">
    Dates are expiry dates. Expiring means within <%= Compliance::EXPIRING_WINDOW %> days; lapses on project means it expires before the project ends.
    Confirmed fake means a person checked it with the issuer and it wasn't found or didn't match; it counts as not valid and is left out of packets.
    A <span class="<%= ComplianceHelper::REVIEW_MARKER_CLASSES %>">Review</span> mark means an automatic check or QR code found a problem; the certificate still counts by its dates until someone checks it with the issuer.
  </p>
</div>
